From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josip Seketa <josip.seketa@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:27:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 51/72] gdb/record-full: resume only the stepped thread on a
 non-stop target

After a recorded step, record full resumed every thread on a non-stop target; remote.c asserted.

diff --git a/gdb/record-full.c b/gdb/record-full.c
index 7b1d64069c7..ea96dd11a64 100644
--- a/gdb/record-full.c
+++ b/gdb/record-full.c
@@ -1298,7 +1298,16 @@ record_full_wait_1 (struct target_ops *ops,
 				    "Process record: record_full_wait "
 				    "issuing one more step in the "
 				    "target beneath\n");
-		      ops->beneath ()->resume (ptid, step, GDB_SIGNAL_0);
+
+		      /* An all-stop target stopped all threads for this
+			 event; resume them as they were.  A non-stop
+			 target stopped only the thread that stepped (RET,
+			 now the current thread), and resumes one thread
+			 at a time.  */
+		      ptid_t resume_ptid = (target_is_non_stop_p ()
+					    ? inferior_ptid : ptid);
+		      ops->beneath ()->resume (resume_ptid, step,
+					       GDB_SIGNAL_0);
 		      proc_target->commit_resumed_state = true;
 		      proc_target->commit_resumed ();
 		      proc_target->commit_resumed_state = false;
